  "retained_changes": [
    "Construct the negotiated I16/F32 slice, then share one RenderState::render and callback-reporting block. Remove duplicated source dispatch while preserving one render/report/release per nonempty packet, clock-before-GetBuffer ordering, frame count and flags.",
    "Move the original startup String into the ready channel. Recover it from SendError when the receiver is closed, preserving the existing log message. Remove the clone allocation and copy without adding a production helper or unsafe code."
  ],
  "retention_basis": [
    "The 11-process packet confirmation shows 1.039-1.068x CPU throughput across six quiet packet fixtures with zero allocations. For F32/128 frames: 259.45 -> 246.97 cycles; F32/256: 290.88 -> 272.43; PCM16/256: 330.30 -> 314.86. The final artifact comparison remains faster across the medians, with PCM16/128 effectively unchanged within noise.",
    "Startup thread-entry allocations fall 5 -> 4 with a live receiver and 4 -> 3 with a closed receiver. Requested bytes fall 1454 -> 1344 and 454 -> 344 respectively; reallocations stay at two. No CPU speedup is claimed for native startup because timings are variable."
  ],
  "rejected_change": {
    "candidate": "Collapse saturating multiply/add and the sentinel clamp into one u128 calculation",
    "reason": "Mixed small effects do not demonstrate an overall gain: typical anchor 8.70 -> 8.37 cycles, zero 8.33 -> 8.67, addition saturation 8.09 -> 8.53, multiplication saturation 9.85 -> 8.41. The original clock function was restored and its text is verified equal to the pass baseline."
  },
  "startup_error_storage": {
    "error_len_bytes": 110,
    "original_capacity_bytes": 160,
    "reference_clone_capacity_bytes": 110,
    "forwarded_capacity_bytes": 160,
    "evidence": "Native forwarding/logging regression test prints the capacities of the direct reference error, its clone and the forwarded value. Exact message contents and closed-channel logging match the reference.",
    "tradeoff": "Moving the error retains its existing spare capacity; this fixture returns 50 additional bytes of capacity compared with the removed clone while avoiding the 110-byte clone allocation/copy."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Packet CPU measurements cover quiet software rendering with COM mocks, not complete hardware callbacks, active music/SFX mixes, or audio latency. Measurements vary; the final packet check shows about 0.3-7.2% throughput differences across the fixtures.",
    "Startup CPU and allocation scopes differ as documented. Allocation counts demonstrate one removed String clone; native CPU timings do not establish a startup speedup.",
    "The returned error keeps its original allocation and capacity. Semantic behavior is checked through exact error text, logging, sender lifetime and native stream tests.",
    "Windows 7 was compile-checked and exercised through legacy COM mocks, not run on Windows 7 hardware. Nightly emits an unrelated unused windows-core workspace dependency warning from its standard-library build."
  ],
